:5,"hold":2,"sell":0,"strongSell":0},"analyst_actions":[{"date":"2026-10-27","firm":"BTIG","action":"main","from":"Buy","to":"Buy"},{"date":"2026-10-19","firm":"Canaccord Genuity","action":"main","from":"Buy","to":"Buy"},{"date":"2026-09-24","firm":"BTIG","action":"main","from":"Buy","to":"Buy"}]},"profile":{"sector":"Healthcare","industry":"Diagnostics & Research","summary":"CareDx, Inc. provides solutions for improving outcomes for transplant patients and advancing organ health in the United States and internationally. The company provides AlloSure Kidney, a donor-derived cell-free DNA (dd-cfDNA) solution for kidney transplant patients; AlloMap Heart, a gene expression profiling solution for heart transplant patients; AlloSure Heart, a dd-cfDNA solution for heart transplant patients; and AlloSure Lung, a dd-cfDNA solution for lung transplant patients. It also offers HeartCare, which provides information about distinct biological processes, such as immune quiescence, active injury, acute cellular rejection, and antibody mediated rejection; HistoMap Kidney, a solution that identifies allograft rejection and type of rejection in kidney transplant biopsy tissue; and AlloHeme, a monitoring test that predicts relapse in patients with acute myeloid leukemia and myelodysplastic syndromes. In addition, the company provides QTYPE that enables precision in human leukocyte antigen (HLA) typing; Olerup SSP, which is used to type HLA alleles based on sequence specific primer technology; and Ottr, a transplant patient management software. Further, it offers AlloSeq Tx, a high-resolution HLA typing solution; AlloSeq cfDNA, a surveillance solution to measure dd-cfDNA in blood; AlloSeq HCT, a solution for chimerism testing for stem cell transplant recipients; Allocell, a solution that monitors the pharmacokinetics of engraftment and persistence of cells for patients who have received allogeneic cell therapy; and XynQAPI, MedActionPlan, CareDx pharmacy, AlloHome, and HLA Data Systems software solutions. It has a license agreement with Illumina, Inc. for the distribution, development, and commercialization of NGS products and technologies. The company was formerly known as XDx, Inc. and changed its name to CareDx, Inc. in March 2014. The company was incorporated in 1998 and is headquartered in Brisbane, California.","employees":761,"website":"https://caredx.com","country":"United States","city":"Brisbane","officers":[{"name":"Mr. John Walter Hanna Jr.","title":"President, CEO & Director"},{"name":"Mr. Keith S. Kennedy C.F.A., CPA","title":"CFO & COO"},{"name":"Mr. Jeffrey A. Novack","title":"General Counsel & Secretary"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":18.93,"tpe":29.94,"ps":4.243,"pfcf":28.07,"peg":1.36,"pb":4.477,"ev_ebitda":16.75,"rev_growth":0.1,"eps_growth":0.167,"eps_growth_fwd":0.0928,"eps_growth_next":0.1205,"div_yield":0,"roe":0.01454,"roa":0.02187,"de":41.94,"gross_margin":0.4983,"op_margin":0.04015,"profit_margin":0,"current_ratio":3.084},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":54.67,"sector":18.93,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":33.91,"sector":29.94,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"ps","label":"Price / Sales","v":7.965,"sector":4.243,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"pfcf","label":"Price / FCF","v":32.53,"sector":28.07,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"peg","label":"PEG","v":null,"sector":1.36,"verdict":"—"},{"k":"pb","label":"Price / Book","v":8.532,"sector":4.477,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"de","label":"Debt / Equity (%)","v":4.522,"sector":41.94,"verdict":"Low debt"},{"k":"rev_growth","label":"Revenue growth","v":0.522,"sector":0.1,"verdict":"Strong"},{"k":"eps_growth","label":"EPS growth (last qtr, y/y)","v":null,"sector":0.167,"verdict":"—"},{"k":"eps_growth_fwd","label":"EPS growth (this year, est.)","v":1.066,"sector":0.0928,"verdict":"Strong"},{"k":"eps_growth_next","label":"EPS growth (next year, est.)","v":0.0765,"sector":0.1205,"verdict":"Weak"},{"k":"gross_margin","label":"Gross margin","v":0.70